Comment: The Sound Manager's downloadable catalog (src/sound_library.rs)
 references dozens of sounds from GNOME Clocks, AOSP, and KDE
 Plasma/Plasma Mobile under CC0-1.0, CC-BY-3.0, CC-BY-4.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0,
 and Apache-2.0. None of them are bundled in this package or fetched
 during the build — they're downloaded on request, into the user's own
 data directory, only if that specific sound is selected, and none are
 pre-selected or otherwise provided by default. Each carries its own
 attribution and license inside the app itself (an info popover on its
 row in the Sound Manager), sourced individually from each project's own
 credits/license files rather than assumed. See sound_library.rs's own
 `default_catalog` function for the complete, per-entry breakdown.

Comment: This package's Rust dependencies (declared in Cargo.toml, not
 vendored into this source package) are fetched from crates.io at build
 time under their own individual licenses — predominantly MIT and/or
 Apache-2.0, the Rust ecosystem's near-universal convention, though this
 isn't exhaustively verified per-crate here. Inspect the exact set with
 `cargo license` (from the cargo-license crate) against Cargo.lock for a
 complete, current accounting if needed.

